@* The app's one small activity indicator (19-11-26, Apple-style streamlining item 5): in a button
   while it works, beside a live status line, or in a search box. It takes the colour of the text
   around it, and with Reduce Motion it pulses gently instead of spinning. Pages and panels that are
   loading use LoadingIndicator (the boot screen); a long job uses BusyOverlay.
   Label: what a screen reader hears. Leave it empty when the text beside it already says it. *@

<span class="gws-progress @CssClass" role="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Label) ? null : "status")"
      aria-hidden="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Label) ? "true" : null)"><span class="visually-hidden">@Label</span></span>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? CssClass { get; set; }
}
